cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, cite it as below. If you use the frozen Jira cache
  archive, cite the Zenodo deposit instead, once minted — see
  deposit/DEPOSIT_CHECKLIST.md.
title: >-
  Traceability and estimate coverage as corpus-eligibility constraints:
  a probe of 38 Apache projects
abstract: >-
  An independent pre-doctoral empirical study of what precedes a developer's
  decision to refactor. 38 Apache projects were probed against a pre-registered
  0.80 commit-side traceability bar; 12 passed, and every one of them was
  incubated at the Apache Software Foundation before the 2019-20 migration of
  ASF projects to GitHub pull requests. The channel the literature publishes —
  what fraction of commits cite a ticket — diverges from the one an
  issue-anchored study needs: what fraction of tickets ever receive a commit.
  The repository carries pre-registered predictions, six hypotheses that failed
  with named causes, a retracted Cox model, a self-corrected aggregation error,
  and an independent adversarial audit of its own numbers.
type: software
